          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Factor the following: (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9a^{2}+b^{2}+4c^{2}-6ab+12ac-4bc"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 6 s ^ { 2 } + 2 5 t ^ { 2 } - 4 0 s t"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "r ^ { 2 }   -   r   -   4 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 9 g ^ { 2 } + 1 4 g h + h ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 4 u ^ { 2 } + 1 2 1 v ^ { 2 } + 4 w ^ { 2 } - 1 7 6 u v - 3 2 u w + 4 4 v w"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.303,
            0.398,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.34,
            0.854,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "James and Reshma were talking about algebraic identities they learnt in school."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.383,
            0.586,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "James: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(a - b)^{2} \\left( a + b \\right) = (a^{2} - 2ab + b^{2})(a + b)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.405,
            0.844,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reshma: I have a different idea. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(a - b)^{2} (a + b) = (a - b) \\left[ (a - b) (a + b) \\right]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (a – b)(a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " – b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ")"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.454,
            0.57,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I will find this product to get the answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.476,
            0.554,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "According to you, who is correct and why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.5,
            0.702,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try to combine more such identities and find new results."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.561,
            0.5,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.7 Finding New Identities"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.595,
            0.886,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this section we will play around with algebraic expressions to see if we can arrive at new identities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.638,
            0.593,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you think "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(a + b)^{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " will look like?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.664,
            0.783,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us find out the answer using the distributive property:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.689,
            0.79,
            0.709
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "(a+b)^{3}=(a+b)(a^{2}+2ab+b^{2})=a^{3}+3a^{2}b+3ab^{2}+b^{3}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.714,
            0.63,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here we have found a new identity, namely,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.739,
            0.554,
            0.759
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "(a + b)^{3} = a^{3} + 3a^{2}b + 3ab^{2} + b^{3}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.765,
            0.667,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us try to visualise this identity. We saw that a square of side "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\; + \\; b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be divided into squares and rectangles. This led us to the identity, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(a^{2}+b)^{2}=a^{2}+2ab+b^{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What if we have a cube of edge "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + b ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Can we divide a cube of edge "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( a + b )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " into smaller cubes and cuboids and represent this new identity?"
            }
          ]
        },
